 "Masahiko Harada"] " " [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"] " / 17 February 1998 / " [:a {:href "/records/event_name/519"} "Details"] [:br {}] [:a {:href "/results/2445"} "137.0"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/96009"} "Takanobu Okabe"] " " [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"] " / 17 February 1998 / " [:a {:href "/records/event_name/519"} "Details"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #1"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5004112"} "Randy Lunde"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #2"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002246"} "Gert Aigmüller"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #3"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002714"} "Janež Frelih"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SLO"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SLO.png"}] "SLO"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #4"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5003126"} "Klaus-Dieter Götze"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #5"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5003132"} "Kolbjørn Asphaug"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "K-Point: 120 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The overwhelming favourite coming in to the Olympics was the 23 year old German " [:a {:href "/athletes/99848"} "Sven Hannawald"] ". Hannawald had done the unprecedented feat of winning all four events of the Four Hills Tournament earlier in the year and was a runaway leader of the World Cup. It was true that he had suffered a shocking defeat to the unheralded Swiss " [:a {:href "/athletes/99870"} "Simon Ammann"] " on the smaller hill but he was expected to bounce back and claim victory in this event. Again Amman proved a thorn in the side of the German favourite and the two man finished dead level after round one with the Pole " [:a {:href "/athletes/99860"} "Adam Małysz"] " in close contact in third. As on the normal hill event it all came down to the final jumps of Ammann and Hannawald to decide the championships. Amman’s leap of 133 m was the best of the competition and heaped the pressure on his German rival. Hannawald could not match the Swiss jumper but his leap of 131 m would have been enough to win the silver medal had he not slipped on landing and lost valuable style points.\nMałysz took a second medal of the games whilst the bronze went to " [:a {:href "/athletes/101136"} "Matti Hautamäki"] ", who upheld Finland’s ski jumping tradition. Ammann, who had never won a World Cup event, thus became the third man to win the individual ski jumping double at an Olympic Winter Games."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/99870"} "Simon Ammann"]] [:td {} [:a {:h